---
import Content from '../layouts/Content.astro';
import { company, site, power, network, compute } from '../data/site';

/* Everything below is arithmetic on the published Phase 1A figures. */
const systems = Number((compute.systems.match(/[\d.]+/) ?? ['0'])[0]);
const gpusPerSystem = compute.gpus / systems;

const loadKw = Number((compute.load.match(/[\d.]+/) ?? ['0'])[0]);
const perSystemKw = loadKw / systems;
---

<Content
  title={`Compute — an eight-GPU first deployment | ${company.full}`}
  description={`${compute.systems} planned at ${site.designation}, ${site.name}. ${compute.gpus} GPUs, ${compute.vramPerGpu} each, ${compute.load}. ${compute.status}.`}
  kicker="Phase 1A hardware"
  heading="Built around your workload."
  lede={`Two planned servers, four ${compute.gpuModel} each, ${compute.vramPerGpu} per GPU. ${compute.status}, and the building it goes into is not yet assigned.`}
  meta={[
    { label: 'Systems', value: String(systems), note: compute.systems, count: true },
    { label: 'GPUs', value: String(compute.gpus), note: `${gpusPerSystem} per system`, count: true },
    { label: 'GPUs planned', value: String(compute.gpus), note: `${compute.vramPerGpu} each, separate memories`, tone: 'signal', count: true },
    { label: 'Estimated IT load', value: compute.load, note: 'Estimated, not measured', tone: 'gold' },
  ]}
>
  <section aria-labelledby="fleet" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">01</span><span class="eyebrow__t">The fleet</span></p>
    <h2 id="fleet">What Phase 1A is</h2>

    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p>
          The first deployment is deliberately small: {compute.systems}, on a
          {' '}{compute.target}. It is planned rather than purchased —
          {' '}{compute.status.toLowerCase()} — and which of Buildings A, B and C takes it
          has not been confirmed.
        </p>
        <p>
          The point of publishing a fleet this size is that every number on this page is
          checkable. A larger announced number would be a forecast; this is a planned
          purchase and a fit-out, and neither has happened yet.
        </p>
        <p>
          All {compute.gpus} GPUs are planned for customer workloads. Nothing is
          designated as held back, which at this size is worth saying plainly: a spares
          reserve would be a quarter of the deployment, and how that is handled is
          {' '}<span class="todo">Spares, acceptance testing and internal allocation will be specified before capacity is offered</span>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <dl class="figures">
        <div>
          <dt>GPUs planned</dt>
          <dd class="is-signal"><span data-count>{compute.gpus}</span><span class="sub">across {systems} planned servers</span></dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Memory per GPU</dt>
          <dd>
            {compute.vramPerGpu}
            <span class="sub">Separate memories — this part has no NVLink</span>
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <blockquote class="pull">
      <p>One deployment, into a building not yet assigned, behind a shared service whose usable IT allocation follows an engineering review.</p>
      <p>
        A larger announced number would be a forecast. This one is a purchase and a
        fit-out, and every figure on the page is checkable against the site record.
      </p>
    </blockquote>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="arithmetic" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">02</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Per system</span></p>
    <h2 id="arithmetic">The power arithmetic, per system</h2>

    <p>
      Accelerated compute is bought in kilowatts as much as in GPUs. Here is the
      published Phase 1A load divided by the published system count, so you can see the
      density this hall has to carry.
    </p>

    <div class="scroller" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Phase 1A per-system arithmetic, scrollable">
      <table>
        <caption>Phase 1A, worked from published figures</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Line</th>
            <th scope="col">Figure</th>
            <th scope="col">Basis</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Systems</th><td class="num">{systems}</td><td>{compute.systems}</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">GPUs per system</th><td class="num">{gpusPerSystem}</td><td>{compute.gpus} GPUs ÷ {systems} systems</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Total IT load</th><td class="num">{compute.load}</td><td>Published Phase 1A draw</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Load per system</th><td class="num">≈ {perSystemKw.toFixed(1)} kW</td><td>Total load ÷ system count</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Rack density</th><td class="num"><span class="todo">Rack layout and density are not yet established</span></td><td>Depends on the final rack layout, which is not fixed</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Memory per GPU</th><td class="num">{compute.vramPerGpu}</td><td>{compute.memoryNote}</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p style="margin-top: var(--s-5);">
      The modeled load per system is a planning input. It does not determine the
      cooling method on its own. The selected server, rack layout and site engineering
      must establish the cooling design and the load that can be commissioned.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="cooling" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">03</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Cooling</span></p>
    <h2 id="cooling">Cooling is not settled yet</h2>

    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p>
          {compute.cooling} — NVIDIA documents both air and liquid options for this part,
          and the selected server governs which applies. Liquid cooling means coolant is carried to a cold plate sitting on the
          package itself, so the majority of the heat leaves the rack as liquid rather
          than as hot air pushed into a containment aisle. It is what makes dense
          accelerator racks practical, and it is far easier to design into a fit-out than
          to retrofit into an operating hall.
        </p>
        <p>
          Building allocation and any cooling upgrades remain subject to the final
          design. Existing HVAC does not establish readiness for the proposed IT load;
          commissioning must verify the selected installation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <dl class="spec">
        <div><dt>Method</dt><dd>{compute.cooling}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>CDU</dt><dd><span class="todo">A CDU specification will be established if the selected cooling design requires one.</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Supply temperature</dt><dd><span class="todo">Supply temperature and temperature rise depend on the selected cooling design.</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Heat rejection</dt><dd><span class="todo">Heat-rejection equipment and water demand are not yet selected.</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Residual air load</dt><dd><span class="todo">Residual air load and supporting HVAC capacity require engineering verification.</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Leak detection</dt><dd><span class="todo">Leak detection and isolation will be specified with any liquid-cooling design.</span></dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="stack" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">04</span><span class="eyebrow__t">The rest of the stack</span></p>
    <h2 id="stack">What we have not specified yet</h2>

    <p>
      The accelerator count is settled. The rest of a training cluster — fabric, storage,
      host configuration, scheduler — is not, and inventing it here would be the fastest
      way to lose a technical buyer in the second meeting. These are the open items.
    </p>

    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Fabric</h3>
        <p>
          <span class="todo">East-west fabric, topology and per-GPU bandwidth await a supported system design and benchmark.</span>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Storage</h3>
        <p>
          <span class="todo">Storage architecture, usable capacity and full-fleet throughput are not yet specified.</span>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Host configuration</h3>
        <p>
          <span class="todo">CPU, system memory and local NVMe will follow the supported OEM configuration.</span>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Software</h3>
        <p>
          <span class="todo">Operating system, drivers, runtime and scheduling will be confirmed for the workload.</span>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Tenancy model</h3>
        <p>
          <span class="todo">Allocation units, virtualization and tenant isolation will be specified before an offer.</span>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>External connectivity</h3>
        <p>
          {network.service} from {network.provider} is planned for the site. {network.status}.
          <span class="todo">Tenant bandwidth and egress policy will be defined in the commercial offer.</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="is-end" aria-labelledby="buying" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">05</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Buying it</span></p>
    <h2 id="buying">How capacity is sold</h2>

    <dl class="spec">
      <div><dt>Available from</dt><dd>{compute.target}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Planned units</dt><dd>{compute.gpus} GPUs across {systems} servers</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Minimum allocation</dt><dd><span class="todo">Minimum GPU or system allocation is subject to workload and commercial review.</span></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Pricing</dt><dd><span class="todo">Pricing and any term discount are quoted after workload and equipment review.</span></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Term</dt><dd><span class="todo">Available term options will be confirmed in the offer.</span></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Support</dt><dd><span class="todo">Replacement commitments, support contacts and coverage hours will be agreed before service.</span></dd></div>
    </dl>

    <p class="form-note">Site and equipment photography will be published when available. Arrange a site visit to verify current conditions; the visual concepts on this page are illustrative.</p>

    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn" href="/contact">Ask what is available</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/colocation">Colocation terms</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Content>
